Fans have spotted Travis Kelce wearing a friendship bracelet with Taylor Swift lyrics on it, just days before she attended his Kansas City Chiefs game.

In a video posted to TikTok on 25 September, a fan shared a photo of Kelce posing with the piece of jewellery on his wrist. The post came after Swift was seen enthusiastically cheering him on in the box seats at Arrowhead Stadium, fuelling speculation that she and the athlete are dating.","entities":["Kansas City Chiefs game","Arrowhead Stadium","Fans spot Travis Kelce wearing Taylor Swift-themed friendship bracelet before she attended his game","friendship bracelet","Taylor Swift","Travis Kelce","TikTok","The Independent","dating","Kansas City Chiefs"],"facts":["Taylor Swift-Travis Kelce timeline: Everything to know about rumored romance between pop star, Chiefs TE -MENTIONS-> Arrowhead Stadium","Travis Kelce faces backlash after comments about ‘finding a breeder’ resurface amid Taylor Swift romance -MENTIONS-> Arrowhead Stadium","When pop culture and sport collide: A timeline of Taylor Swift’s NFL takeover -MENTIONS-> Arrowhead Stadium","Travis Kelce says he tried to delete his ‘nonsense’ tweets before they went viral -MENTIONS-> Arrowhead Stadium","Taylor Swift reveals secret start to her relationship with Travis Kelce -MENTIONS-> Arrowhead Stadium"]}

{"title":"Travis Kelce says he tried to delete his ‘nonsense’ tweets before they went viral (The Independent - Life and Style, 2023-11-25T14:50:53+00:00)","text":"Travis Kelce says he tried to delete his ‘nonsense’ tweets before they went viral (The Independent - Life and Style, 2023-11-25T14:50:53+00:00)
The dating speculation first began in July, when Kelce confessed that he tried and failed to give Swift a friendship bracelet with his number on it during her Eras Tour show. On his podcast, he later invited the “Anti-Hero” singer to one of his games at Arrowhead Stadium - an invitation she famously accepted on 24 September. Since then, Swift has attended three more of Kelce’s games.

Kelce showed his support for Swift when he attended her Eras Tour show in Buenos Aires, Argentina, on 11 November. During the concert, Swift gave a shout-out to the Chiefs player when she changed her “Karma” lyrics to reflect their relationship. “Karma is the guy on the Chiefs, coming straight home to me,” she sang, letting out a laugh as fans in the audience screamed in response. The “All Too Well” singer was later seen running into his arms and kissing the NFL player following the concert, as he whisked her away backstage.","entities":["Arrowhead Stadium","All Too Well","Anti-Hero","Argentina","friendship bracelet","Travis Kelce says he tried to delete his ‘nonsense’ tweets before they went viral","Eras Tour show in Buenos Aires","Buenos Aires","dating speculation","Karma","Taylor Swift","Travis Kelce","Chiefs","The Independent"],"facts":["When pop culture and sport collide: A timeline of Taylor Swift’s NFL takeover -MENTIONS-> Arrowhead Stadium","Fans spot Travis Kelce wearing Taylor Swift-themed friendship bracelet before she attended his game -MENTIONS-> Arrowhead Stadium","Taylor Swift-Travis Kelce timeline: Everything to know about rumored romance between pop star, Chiefs TE -MENTIONS-> Arrowhead Stadium","Travis Kelce faces backlash after comments about ‘finding a breeder’ resurface amid Taylor Swift romance -MENTIONS-> Arrowhead Stadium","Taylor Swift reveals secret start to her relationship with Travis Kelce -MENTIONS-> Arrowhead Stadium"]}

{"title":"The FTX trial is bigger than Sam Bankman-Fried (The Verge, 2023-09-28T12:00:00+00:00)","text":"The FTX trial is bigger than Sam Bankman-Fried (The Verge, 2023-09-28T12:00:00+00:00)
Bankman-Fried is accused of using “billions of dollars in misappropriated FTX customer deposits” to help buy more than $200 million of real estate for himself, make billions of dollars of investments for his own interest, and repay Alameda’s lenders, according to the indictment, Additionally, Bankman-Fried allegedly used more than $100 million of customer funds to make political contributions; prosecutors can show evidence of those contributions in this trial, even though they aren’t part of the charges brought. A second trial is scheduled for March 2024, with additional charges.

Before his fall, Bankman-Fried made himself out to be the Good Boy of crypto — the trustworthy face of a sometimes-shady industry. He was also very interested in publicity, sitting for many interviews both before and after the fall of FTX. The quick rise of FTX as an industry force was at least in part due to Bankman-Fried’s appetite for attention.","entities":["crypto","Alameda","FTX trial","second trial","misappropriated FTX customer deposits","political contributions","The FTX trial is bigger than Sam Bankman-Fried","real estate","FTX","Sam Bankman-Fried","The Verge"],"facts":["SBF’s trial starts soon, but how did he — and FTX — get here? -MENTIONS-> crypto","SBF, riding high on FTX, reportedly offered $5B to Trump to cancel President re-run -MENTIONS-> crypto","Is Sam Bankman-Fried a bad ‘man’ or a good ‘boy’? Lawyers swap opening statements before first witnesses take the stand -MENTIONS-> crypto","Sam Bankman-Fried was a terrible boyfriend -MENTIONS-> crypto","SBF Trial: The latest updates from the FTX collapse’s courtroom drama -MENTIONS-> crypto"]}

{"title":"The FTX trial is bigger than Sam Bankman-Fried (The Verge, 2023-09-28T12:00:00+00:00)","text":"The FTX trial is bigger than Sam Bankman-Fried (The Verge, 2023-09-28T12:00:00+00:00)
If it seems like his peer group supported him, or worse, fawned over him, that’s a real problem for the industry’s reputation.”

After FTX declared bankruptcy, Bankman-Fried went on an extensive media tour, doing interviews with The New York Times’ Andrew Ross Sorkin and Good Morning America. Even under house arrest, he did interviews, including with The New Yorker. Bankman-Fried seemed to think that if he just explained things, everyone would understand that what he did was a mistake, not a crime.","entities":["The New York Times","FTX trial","The FTX trial is bigger than Sam Bankman-Fried","extensive media tour","interviews","Andrew Ross Sorkin","Good Morning America","The New Yorker","FTX","Sam Bankman-Fried","The Verge"],"facts":["He’s Hockey’s Brightest Young Star. This Is What Makes His Shot So Special. -PUBLISHED_BY-> The New York Times","How U.S. Women’s Soccer Team Lured Emma Hayes Away From Chelsea -PUBLISHED_BY-> The New York Times","After a Stunning Snub, College Football Is Facing an Identity Crisis -PUBLISHED_BY-> The New York Times","N.F.L. Executives on the Biggest Questions Facing Super Bowl Contenders -PUBLISHED_BY-> The New York Times","Which M.L.B. Playoff Team Has the Most Daunting Home Field? We Ranked Them. -PUBLISHED_BY-> The New York Times"]}

{"title":"The jury finally hears from Sam Bankman-Fried (The Verge, 2023-10-28T00:12:41+00:00)","text":"The jury finally hears from Sam Bankman-Fried (The Verge, 2023-10-28T00:12:41+00:00)
When he found it, he was “very surprised!”

Besides the two obvious lies Bankman-Fried told on the stand — about Alameda Research’s name and about “allow_negative” — I have been struck by how little he seems to know about his own companies. Apparently, Singh, Wang, and Ellison were out there just doing whatever their little hearts desired. Because Bankman-Fried was a CEO, but definitely not the kind that pays any attention to money at his crypto trading firm and futures exchange.","entities":["The jury finally hears from Sam Bankman-Fried","Alameda Research","allow_negative","Ellison","Singh","Wang","Sam Bankman-Fried","The Verge"],"facts":["The jury finally hears from Sam Bankman-Fried -MENTIONS-> Gary Wang","The jury finally hears from Sam Bankman-Fried -MENTIONS-> Caroline Ellison","The jury finally hears from Sam Bankman-Fried -MENTIONS-> Mark Cohen","The jury finally hears from Sam Bankman-Fried -MENTIONS-> Adam Yedidia","The jury finally hears from Sam Bankman-Fried -MENTIONS-> Securities and Exchange Commission"]}

